{"orgCode":"6125","name":"Education Audit Appeals Panel","agencyCode":"6010","agencyName":"K thru 12 Education","description":"The Education Audit Appeals Panel (EAAP) serves as the neutral arbiter in formal and informal administrative audit appeals by TK-12 local educational agencies (LEAs), may approve settlements and make findings of fact and interpretations of law, and applies where appropriate, a statutorily defined test of substantial compliance with respect to audit appeals by TK-12 LEAs. Additionally, the EAAP adopts as regulations, according to a statutory timetable, the audit guide used in annual audits, which includes appendices for Local School Construction Bond Audits, School Facility Program Bond Fund Audits, and Full-Day Kindergarten Facilities Grant Program Audits. The EAAP's mission is to set clear standards for compliance with education funding requirements and avoid lengthy and expensive litigation over disputed funding between the state and LEAs. The EAAP's membership consists of the State Superintendent of Public Instruction, the Director of Finance, and the Chief Executive Officer of the County Office Fiscal Crisis and Management Assistance Team, or their designees.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":938,"cy":1369,"by":1171},"positions":{"py":3,"cy":5.3,"by":5.3}},"programs":{"id":"exp/6010/6125","kind":"department","name":"Education Audit Appeals Panel","code":"6125","amounts":{"py":938,"cy":1369,"by":1171},"positions":{"py":3,"cy":5.3,"by":5.3},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":938,"cy":1369,"by":1171}},"children":[{"id":"exp/6010/6125/5320","kind":"program","name":"Education Audit Appeals Panel","code":"5320","amounts":{"py":938,"cy":1369,"by":1171},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":938,"cy":1369,"by":1171}},"positions":{"py":3,"cy":5.3,"by":5.3},"extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":938,"cy":1369,"by":1171}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/6010/6125/5320/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"p